<title>CHINA: China 1997 toluene shortfall seen at 200,000 T.</title>
<headline>China 1997 toluene shortfall seen at 200,000 T.</headline>
<dateline>BEIJING 1997-06-19</dateline>
<text>
<p>China should this year import toluene, also known as methyl benzene, to make up an expected 200,000 tonne shortfall in supply of the liquid hydrocarbon, the China Chemical Industry News said on Thursday.</p>
<p>Chinese demand for toluene would be 600,000 tonnes in 1997, the newspaper said.</p>
<p>Demand was well above expected output, despite annual increases in production of over 15 percent over the last several years, it said but gave no figures or further details.</p>
<p>Toluene is a colourless flammable hydrocarbon used to make such products as dyes and explosives.</p>
<p>-- Beijing Newsroom (8610) 6532 1921</p>
</text>
